<% @wide = true %>
<h1>What the page actually did</h1>

<p class="lede">
    Not a description of the problem — the element, the rule that styled
    it, and the browser it happened in.
</p>

<figure class="specimen">
    <figcaption>Every visual report carries this</figcaption>
    <ol class="cascade">
        <li class="is-layer">@layer components</li>
        <li class="is-condition">@media (width &gt; 20rem)</li>
        <li class="is-selector">.caption
            <span class="where">/common/style/exhibition-standard.css</span>
        </li>
    </ol>
</figure>

<h2>Take it with you</h2>

<p>
    Drag this to your bookmarks toolbar, or right-click and choose
    <em>Bookmark link</em>. Pasting a <code>javascript:</code> URL into
    the address bar will not work — browsers strip it.
</p>

<p><a class="bookmarklet" href="#">Corrigenda</a></p>

<details>
    <summary>Copy the URL instead</summary>
    <pre class="bookmarklet-source"></pre>
</details>

<h2>Or install the add-on</h2>

<p>
    The add-on does two things the bookmarklet cannot. Its toolbar
    button puts the widget on any page of the estate, so there is
    nothing to drag anywhere. And it photographs the tab through the
    browser's own capture API: no share dialog, no picking the right
    window, and a frame that is already in page coordinates — which is
    what lets a screenshot be cropped to the element and masked over
    form fields.
</p>

<dl class="packages">
    <% [["firefox", "Firefox",
         "Captures any rectangle of the page, including the part " \
         "below the fold, so “no crop” really is the whole page.",
         "about:debugging → This Firefox → Load Temporary Add-on, and " \
         "pick manifest.json inside the unzipped folder. A permanent " \
         "install needs the package signed."],
        ["chrome", "Chrome",
         "Captures the visible page only — Chrome has no API for the " \
         "part below the fold — but the crop to the element and the " \
         "masking both work.",
         "chrome://extensions → Developer mode → Load unpacked, and " \
         "pick the unzipped folder."]].each do |target, name, what, how| %>
        <div>
            <dt><%= name %></dt>
            <dd>
                <p><%= what %></p>
                <% if (bytes = packages[target]) %>
                    <p>
                        <a class="package" href="<%= mount("/extension/#{target}") %>"
                           download>Download for <%= name %></a>
                        <span class="weight"><%= (bytes / 1024.0).round %> kB</span>
                    </p>
                    <p class="how"><%= how %></p>
                <% else %>
                    <p class="empty">
                        Not built yet. Run <code>extension/build <%= target %></code>
                        where this service lives.
                    </p>
                <% end %>
            </dd>
        </div>
    <% end %>
</dl>

<h2>Four kinds of report</h2>

<p>
    The kind sets what gets collected and how you point at the problem.
    The marks are what it switches on for you; every one of them is
    still yours to change before sending.
</p>

<%
    # The defaults the widget applies, in the same order and the same
    # letters it shows on its own menu — WANTED in the client.
    kinds = [
        ["Visual", "how it looks",
         %w[fragment rules computed diagnostics audit screenshot],
         "The element, the rules that matched it and the layer or media " \
         "query they came from, computed styles, geometry, the " \
         "accessibility check, and the screenshot control. For overlap, " \
         "spacing, colour, a layout that breaks at a width."],

        ["Content", "the words are wrong",
         %w[fragment],
         "Wording, typos, a stale fact. <strong>Select the text " \
         "first</strong> and the picker is skipped: the words are quoted " \
         "into the message and the elements holding them are recorded. " \
         "The element and nothing else — computed styles say nothing " \
         "about a spelling mistake."],

        ["Broken", "it does not work",
         %w[fragment diagnostics],
         "Behaviour rather than appearance: a control that does nothing, " \
         "an image that never arrives, a script that threw. Adds the " \
         "JavaScript errors and failed loads collected since the page " \
         "opened, and whether it overflows sideways."],

        ["Idea", "suggestion or question",
         [],
         "No element, no picker, no capture. The message and the page " \
         "you were on."]
    ]
%>

<dl class="kinds">
    <% kinds.each do |name, purpose, channels, what| %>
        <div>
            <dt><%= name %><span class="purpose"><%= purpose %></span></dt>
            <dd>
                <p class="marks">
                    <% if channels.empty? %>
                        <span class="empty">nothing but the message</span>
                    <% else %>
                        <% channels.each do |key| %>
                            <span class="chip" data-channel="<%= key %>"
                                  title="<%= Corrigenda::CHANNELS[key][1] %>"><%=
                                  Corrigenda::CHANNELS[key][0] %></span>
                        <% end %>
                    <% end %>
                </p>
                <p><%== what %></p>
            </dd>
        </div>
    <% end %>
</dl>

<%# The same legend the reports list carries, and the same letters the
    widget puts on its own menu: six marks learned once. %>
<dl class="legend">
    <% Corrigenda::CHANNELS.each do |key, (mark, label)| %>
        <dt><span class="chip" data-channel="<%= key %>"><%= mark %></span></dt>
        <dd><%= label %></dd>
    <% end %>
</dl>

<h2>Driving it</h2>

<dl class="kinds is-three">
    <div>
        <dt>Picking<span class="purpose">point at the problem</span></dt>
        <dd>
            <%# The same three hues the picker outlines the page with,
                and the same ones on its own help bar: a key is dressed
                as the box it will draw, so the colour is read rather
                than remembered. %>
            <p class="marks">
                <kbd class="k-parent">↑</kbd> parent
                <kbd class="k-child">↓</kbd> child
                <kbd class="k-sibling">←</kbd>
                <kbd class="k-sibling">→</kbd> siblings
            </p>
            <p>
                Click the element; the arrow keys walk the tree from
                there, because what you want is usually the container
                and not the leaf the mouse can reach.
                <kbd>Enter</kbd> locks it, <kbd>Esc</kbd> cancels — and
                a drag draws a region instead.
            </p>
        </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
        <dt>Sending<span class="purpose">nothing you did not see</span></dt>
        <dd>
            <p>
                Each channel is a switch showing its own size, and
                <em>what will be sent</em> renders the exact payload
                before it goes. Form values, password fields and
                anything marked
                <code>data-corrigenda-redact</code> never leave the
                page.
            </p>
        </dd>
    </div>

    <div>
        <dt>Screenshots<span class="purpose">your real rendering</span></dt>
        <dd>
            <p>
                Taken through the browser's own capture permission, so
                the image is the page as it actually drew — not a
                redrawing of how it was meant to look. Cropping to the
                element and the bars over form fields need a frame that
                maps to the page: share <strong>this tab</strong>, or
                install the add-on and skip the question.
            </p>
        </dd>
    </div>
</dl>

<h2>Where it works</h2>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Reports about</dt>
    <dd>
        <% if sites.nil? %>
            Any site — no allowlist configured.
        <% else %>
            <% sites.each do |site| %>
                <code><%= site %></code><br>
            <% end %>
            <p>What a report may claim to be about. One naming anything
            else is refused.</p>
        <% end %>
    </dd>

    <dt>Posted from</dt>
    <dd>
        <% if origins.nil? %>
            Any origin — no allowlist configured.
        <% else %>
            <% origins.each do |origin| %>
                <code><%= origin %></code><br>
            <% end %>
            <p>Which pages may send one from another host. A page
            elsewhere is stopped by its own browser: the answer to the
            preflight does not name it.</p>
        <% end %>
    </dd>

    <% if endpoint %>
        <dt>Point a site here</dt>
        <dd>
            <p>A site that does not mount this service names it before
            the vertical bar, and says who gets the widget after it:</p>
            <pre><code>&lt;m:framework corrigenda="<%= endpoint.sub(%r{/\.corrigenda\z}, "") %>|yes"/&gt;</code></pre>
            <p>A site that does mount it (<code>Use
            CorrigendaEndpoint</code> in its vhost) leaves the
            endpoint out and posts to its own origin, which needs no
            CORS.</p>
        </dd>
    <% end %>
</dl>

<h2>State</h2>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Reports</dt>
    <dd><a href="<%= mount("/review/") %>"><%= count %> stored</a></dd>

    <dt>Latest</dt>
    <dd><%= latest ? "#{latest["at"]} — #{latest["url"]}" : "Nothing reported yet." %></dd>

    <dt>Store</dt>
    <dd><code><%= store_path %></code></dd>

    <dt>Endpoint</dt>
    <dd><a href="<%= mount("/report/health") %>">health</a></dd>
</dl>

<script>
    /* The app is behind a proxy and is not told its public URL. The
       browser knows it: this page came from it. */
    (function () {
        var src = location.origin + "<%= mount("/corrigenda.js") %>";
        var code = "javascript:(function(){var s=document.createElement('script');" +
                   "s.src='" + src + "';document.body.appendChild(s);})();";
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet").href = code;
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet-source").textContent = code;
    })();
</script>
